        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-03T15:02:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is a good point. I was hedging my bets and thinking we might need a wrapper that makes it easy to move between uint16_t, 24-bit, or a float value, and also wanted to differentiate it from the uint16_t that stored the buffer sort indices for the draw. But \"ZValue depth\" or \"ZValue zvalue\" is not very meaningful at all. Would you be okay with something like \"Depth writeValue\" so that it\u0027s clear it goes into the depth buffer and is also what the draw uses when writing to the depth buffer?\n\nOn a similar note, I am now questioning my choice of name for BufferIndex. It could be easily misinterpreted as an index into a multi-render target setup, whereas it is really value to sort on. Maybe just BufferSortIndex? BufferConstraint? wdyt?",
      "parentUuid": "ce74f975_ac0cbb76",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 40
      },
